From 50ec66f75d57ad55838a9fe4da5e66f29af4d73c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brit <10531428+H4vC@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:34:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ai): show Anthropic between-tool narration as reply text

Opus 5.5 returns prose written between tool calls as a signed thinking block whose signature header kind is "narration", so mid-task replies folded into the Thought block. Flag those blocks (ThinkingContent.narration, read from the signature header like Claude Code does, no length cap) and present them as answer text in the TUI, streaming reveal, print mode, ACP, and HTML export; replay keeps them as signed thinking.
